AXIS ERROR+
      +/@1@⍳3
      ^^

      )MORE
Invalid Token type for function axis.
      )SIC

      ⍝ regression (Bugs28 #91): two bracket axes on a reduce or scan
      ⍝ were both accepted, with the FIRST one silently discarded --
      ⍝ DerivedFunction::eval_XB()'s monadic branch always preferred the
      ⍝ call-time axis over a member axis already baked in at parse
      ⍝ time (e.g. by "+/[1]" itself), instead of rejecting the
      ⍝ redundant second axis the way every other two-axis form (,/¨,
      ⍝ 1⌷, a derived operator via ⍤, three axes) already does.
      ⍝
